<title>USA: 3Com sees financial &quot;challenge&quot; from buy.</title>
<headline>3Com sees financial &quot;challenge&quot; from buy.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>3Com Corp will face a short-term financial &quot;challenge&quot; following the $6.6 billion acquisition of US Robotics Corp, 3Com's chief financial officer said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;When you do a transaction of this size, you always get disruptions,&quot; Chris Paisley told investors in San Francisco.</p>
<p>Paisley said, however, the acquisition would be &quot;neutral or slightly accretive&quot; to earnings per share in fiscal 1998.</p>
<p>Paisley did not specify the impact of the acquisition in coming quarters. But the company will take a significant charge in the quarter that the acquisition is completed, expected to be in early summer.</p>
</text>
